error[DZ0557]: `shout` cannot have type parameters of its own
     ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:1006:22
     │
1006 │     virtual fn shout<T>(&self, v: T) {
     │                      ^ a type parameter of the method
     │
     = help: a `virtual` method has one slot in the vtable, and an instance per type argument would need one each; take the varying part as a trait reference instead (spec §7.3, §8.1)

error[DZ0557]: `show` cannot have type parameters of its own
     ┌─ typeerrors/src/errors.dz:1012:13
     │
1012 │     fn show<T>(&self, v: T)
     │             ^ a type parameter of the method
     │
     = help: a trait's method is called through implementations the caller may not know, and through `^Trait` with no type at all; make the trait generic instead, `trait Show<T>` (spec §7.6, §8.1)

